        "text": "\nClaude finished the response\nSearched the web\nHC (Ministerial) / Havildar (Clerk) के लिए Typing test:\n\nSpeed: English में 35 शब्द प्रति मिनट या Hindi में 30 शब्द प्रति मिनट। यानी English में 10,500 और Hindi में 9,000 key depressions प्रति घंटा। आपको दोनों में से एक भाषा चुननी होती है।\nसमय: 10 मिनट का passage।\nError की छूट: करीब 5% गलती चलती है (एक source में 10% लिखा है, इसलिए notification में देख लेना)। इससे ज़्यादा हर गलती पर 10 शब्द कटते हैं।\nHindi का font और layout: कई sites के हिसाब से Hindi में Mangal font और Remington Gail या Inscript layout चलता है। आपको कौन सा layout मिलेगा, यह skill test के instructions में देख लेना।\nBackspace: कई sites कहती हैं कि exam software में backspace बंद होता है। इसकी पुष्टि admit card या skill test के instruction से कर लेना।\nASI (Steno) / Warrant Officer (PA) के लिए: typing की जगह stenography test होता है। एक source के हिसाब से transcription English में 50 मिनट और Hindi में 65 मिनट में करनी होती है। Dictation की speed मुझे किसी भरोसेमंद जगह से नहीं मिली, वह notification में देखनी पड़ेगी।\n\nयह test qualifying है, यानी इसके marks merit में नहीं जुड़ते, बस पास होना ज़रूरी है। पास न हुए तो आगे नहीं जा सकते।\n\nतैयारी के लिए:\n\nरोज़ 10 मिनट का पूरा test बिना backspace के practice करो।\nSpeed से ज़्यादा accuracy पर ध्यान दो, क्योंकि हर एक्स्ट्रा गलती 10 शब्द खा जाती है।\nजिस भाषा में आपकी speed बेहतर हो, वही चुनना।\nआपने Steno और HCM दोनों में से किस post के लिए apply किया था, और English या Hindi typing में से कौन सी आपकी अच्छी है? बता दो, तो उसी हिसाब से practice plan बना दूँगा।\n\nएक बात और: अगर आप CBT के बाद typing test तक पहुँचे, तो call letter rectt.bsf.gov.in पर आएगा, इसलिए वहाँ नज़र रखना।\n\nHINDI ME TYPING H ISME ?/\n\nहाँ, Hindi typing का option है। आप English या Hindi में से एक चुन सकते हो। दोनों में से किसी एक में पास होना काफी है।\n\nHindi typing की शर्त:\n\n30 शब्द प्रति मिनट (9,000 key depressions प्रति घंटा)\n10 मिनट का test\n5% गलती की छूट, उससे ज़्यादा हर गलती पर 10 शब्द कटेंगे\nFont और keyboard layout: ज़्यादातर sites Mangal font लिखती हैं। Layout को लेकर sites अलग-अलग बात बताती हैं: कोई Remington Gail कहती है, कोई Inscript। इसलिए test के दिन कौन सा layout मिलेगा, यह call letter या skill test के instructions में देख लेना, और उसी layout पर practice करना।\n\nHindi में 30 शब्द प्रति मिनट आमतौर पर English के 35 से थोड़ा आसान पड़ता है, ख़ासकर अगर आपको Hindi layout की आदत है। आपको Hindi typing आती है, या अभी सीखनी पड़ेगी?\n\nENSGLISH ME KRNA H M\n\nUpdated memory\nठीक है, English typing में 35 शब्द प्रति मिनट चाहिए, 10 मिनट में, यानी करीब 350 शब्द। 5% तक गलती चलती है, उससे ऊपर हर गलती पर 10 शब्द कटते हैं।\n\nTarget क्या रखें:\n\nअसली test में घबराहट और नई keyboard की वजह से speed थोड़ी गिरती है। इसलिए practice में 40-45 WPM का target रखो, तब 35 आराम से निकल जाएगा।\nAccuracy 97% या उससे ऊपर रखो।\nPractice कैसे करें:\n\nरोज़ 10 मिनट का पूरा test दो, वो भी बिना backspace के। Official software में backspace बंद बताया जाता है, इसलिए यह आदत ज़रूरी है (पक्का करने के लिए call letter देख लेना)।\nएक बार में सिर्फ speed या सिर्फ accuracy पर मत भागो। पहले accuracy पक्की करो, speed अपने आप बढ़ेगी।\nPaper से देखकर screen पर type करने की practice करो, क्योंकि BSF में अक्सर छपा हुआ passage दिया जाता है (यह भी instructions में confirm कर लेना)।\nसही finger placement (home row) रखो और keyboard पर मत देखो।\nPunctuation और capital letters पर ध्यान दो, क्योंकि वे भी गलती गिने जाते हैं।\nरोज़ का plan:\n\n15 मिनट: home row और कठिन keys की drill\n10 मिनट: पूरा 10 मिनट का test\n5 मिनट: अपनी गलतियों को देखकर सुधारना\nअभी आपकी English typing speed लगभग कितनी है? बता दो, तो उसी हिसाब से बता दूँगा कि 35 तक पहुँचने में कितना समय लगेगा।\n\nhttps://github.com/ajaynxt/typing- IS REPO KO THIK KR KE DO\n\nRead 2 pages, ran a command, shared files\nFetched: GitHub - ajaynxt/typing-\nhttps://github.com/ajaynxt/typing-\nPresented file\n\nIndex\nCode·HTML \nhttps://github.com/ajaynxt/typing-/tree/main ME KRNAA H\n\nFailed to send. A retry control is available on the message.\n\nYou are out of free messages until 10:00 PM\nhttps://github.com/ajaynxt/typing-/tree/main ME KRNAA H\n\nClaude is AI and can make mistakes.\n\n\nIndex · HTML\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"utf-8\" />\n  <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width,initial-scale=1\" />\n  <title>TypeMaster • 5 Minute Typing Test</title>\n  <meta name=\"description\" content=\"A clean 5-minute typing practice website with WPM, accuracy, mistakes, and progress tracking.\" />\n  <style>\n    :root{--bg:#0b0d10;--panel:#12161b;--panel2:#171c22;--text:#f4f6f8;--muted:#8f99a6;--line:#252c34;--accent:#d8ff4f;--danger:#ff6b6b;--ok:#8ff0bb;--shadow:0 20px 60px rgba(0,0,0,.28)}\n    *{box-sizing:border-box} html{scroll-behavior:smooth} body{margin:0;background:radial-gradient(circle at 50% -20%,#1b222b 0,#0b0d10 42%);color:var(--text);font-family:Inter,ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,\"Segoe UI\",sans-serif;min-height:100vh}\n    .wrap{width:min(1120px,calc(100% - 32px));margin:auto}.topbar{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;padding:28px 0}.brand{display:flex;gap:10px;align-items:center;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:-.03em}.mark{width:34px;height:34px;border:1px solid #3b444e;border-radius:10px;display:grid;place-items:center;background:#10141a}.mark span{font-size:17px;color:var(--accent)}.pill{font-size:12px;color:var(--muted);border:1px solid var(--line);padding:8px 11px;border-radius:999px}\n    .hero{padding:34px 0 18px}.eyebrow{color:var(--accent);font-size:12px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase}.hero h1{font-size:clamp(42px,7vw,78px);line-height:.95;margin:12px 0;letter-spacing:-.055em;max-width:800px}.hero p{color:var(--muted);font-size:17px;max-width:650px;line-height:1.6;margin:0}\n    .controls{display:flex;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:30px 0}.control{background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:14px;padding:10px}.control label{display:block;font-size:11px;color:var(--muted);margin:0 0 6px 4px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.08em}.control select,.control button{font:inherit;color:var(--text);background:transparent;border:0;padding:7px 8px;outline:none}.control button{cursor:pointer}.control button:hover{color:var(--accent)}\n    .stats{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:12px;margin:16px 0 14px}.stat{background:rgba(18,22,27,.82);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:18px;padding:18px 20px;box-shadow:var(--shadow)}.stat .label{font-size:12px;color:var(--muted);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.08em}.stat .value{font-size:32px;font-weight:750;letter-spacing:-.04em;margin-top:5px}\n    .test{background:rgba(18,22,27,.92);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:24px;overflow:hidden;box-shadow:var(--shadow)}.testhead{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;padding:16px 20px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}.mode{font-size:13px;color:var(--muted)}.timer{font-size:27px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:-.04em}.timer.urgent{color:#ffd166}.timer.done{color:var(--danger)}\n    .typing-area{padding:28px 24px}.quote{white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:24px;line-height:1.8;letter-spacing:.008em;min-height:230px;max-height:560px;overflow:auto;color:#707a86;user-select:none;padding-right:8px}.quote .para{display:block;margin:0 0 24px}.quote .para:last-child{margin-bottom:0}.quote span{position:relative}.quote .current{color:var(--text);border-left:2px solid var(--accent);padding-left:1px}.quote .correct{color:var(--ok)}.quote .wrong{color:var(--danger);text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-thickness:2px;text-underline-offset:5px}.quote .cursor{border-left:2px solid var(--accent);animation:blink 1s step-end infinite}@keyframes blink{50%{border-color:transparent}}\n    .inputwrap{margin-top:24px}.typing-input{width:100%;min-height:78px;resize:none;background:#0e1216;color:#eef2f5;border:1px solid #303943;border-radius:15px;padding:18px;font:inherit;font-size:18px;outline:none}.typing-input:focus{border-color:#65717f;box-shadow:0 0 0 4px rgba(216,255,79,.06)}.hint{color:var(--muted);font-size:12px;margin-top:10px}.actions{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;padding:0 24px 24px}.primary{background:var(--accent);color:#0b0d10;font-weight:800;border:0;border-radius:12px;padding:12px 18px;cursor:pointer}.secondary{background:transparent;color:var(--text);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px;padding:11px 16px;cursor:pointer}.secondary:hover{border-color:#46515c}\n    .result{display:none;padding:26px 24px;border-top:1px solid var(--line);background:#0f1317}.result.show{display:block}.result h2{margin:0 0 18px;font-size:26px}.resultgrid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:12px}.resultcard{border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:14px;padding:15px}.resultcard .big{font-size:27px;font-weight:800;margin-top:4px}.small{font-size:12px;color:var(--muted)}\n    .progress{height:8px;background:#20262d;border-radius:99px;overflow:hidden;margin:16px 0}.bar{height:100%;width:0;background:var(--accent);transition:width .15s linear}\n    .adslot{margin:18px 0 20px;min-height:92px;border:1px dashed #303943;border-radius:16px;background:rgba(14,18,22,.72);display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;overflow:hidden}.adslot .adlabel{font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#65717f}.adsbygoogle{display:block;width:100%;min-height:90px}\n    .footer{padding:28px 0 44px;color:#707983;font-size:12px;text-align:center}.kbd{border:1px solid #333d47;border-bottom-width:2px;border-radius:6px;padding:2px 6px;color:#bdc5ce}\n    @media(max-width:850px){.stats,.resultgrid{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr)}.quote{font-size:20px;line-height:1.72}.hero h1{max-width:680px}}@media(max-width:560px){.wrap{width:min(100% - 20px,1120px)}.topbar{padding:18px 0}.pill{display:none}.hero{padding-top:24px}.hero h1{font-size:44px}.hero p{font-size:15px}.stats{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr)}.stat{padding:15px}.stat .value{font-size:27px}.testhead{padding:14px 15px}.typing-area{padding:22px 15px}.quote{font-size:18px;min-height:245px}.actions{padding:0 15px 15px;gap:10px;flex-direction:column-reverse;align-items:stretch}.primary,.secondary{width:100%}}\n  </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n  <div class=\"wrap\">\n    <header class=\"topbar\">\n      <div class=\"brand\"><div class=\"mark\"><span>⌁</span></div><div>TypeMaster</div></div>\n      <div class=\"pill\">5:00 test • local progress</div>\n    </header>\n \n    <section class=\"hero\">\n      <div class=\"eyebrow\">Typing practice</div>\n      <h1>Build speed.<br>Keep accuracy.</h1>\n      <p>A focused five-minute typing session with live WPM, accuracy, errors, and a clean result summary.</p>\n    </section>\n \n    <div class=\"adslot\" aria-label=\"Advertisement\"><div class=\"adlabel\">Advertisement</div></div>\n \n    <div class=\"controls\">\n      <div class=\"control\"><label>Language</label><select id=\"language\"><option value=\"en\">English</option><option value=\"hi\">Hindi</option></select></div>\n      <div class=\"control\"><label>Duration</label><select id=\"duration\"><option value=\"600\">10 minutes</option><option value=\"300\" selected>5 minutes</option><option value=\"120\">2 minutes</option><option value=\"60\">1 minute</option></select></div>\n      <div class=\"control\"><label>Level</label><select id=\"level\"><option value=\"easy\">Easy</option><option value=\"medium\" selected>Medium</option><option value=\"hard\">Hard</option></select></div>\n      <div class=\"control\"><label>Action</label><button id=\"newText\">New text ↻</button></div>\n    </div>\n \n    <section class=\"stats\">\n      <div class=\"stat\"><div class=\"label\">WPM</div><div class=\"value\" id=\"wpm\">0</div></div>\n      <div class=\"stat\"><div class=\"label\">Accuracy</div><div class=\"value\" id=\"accuracy\">100%</div></div>\n      <div class=\"stat\"><div class=\"label\">Errors</div><div class=\"value\" id=\"errors\">0</div></div>\n      <div class=\"stat\"><div class=\"label\">Time</div><div class=\"value\" id=\"time\">5:00</div></div>\n    </section>\n \n    <section class=\"test\">\n      <div class=\"testhead\"><div><div class=\"mode\" id=\"modeLabel\">English • Medium</div><div class=\"small\" id=\"corpusInfo\" style=\"margin-top:4px\">34K+ characters • randomized paragraphs</div></div><div class=\"timer\" id=\"timer\">5:00</div></div>\n      <div class=\"typing-area\">\n        <div class=\"quote\" id=\"quote\" aria-label=\"Typing text\"></div>\n        <div class=\"inputwrap\">\n          <textarea id=\"input\" class=\"typing-input\" spellcheck=\"false\" autocomplete=\"off\" autocapitalize=\"off\" placeholder=\"Start typing here…\"></textarea>\n          <div class=\"hint\">Tip: start typing to begin. <span class=\"kbd\">Backspace</span> is disabled, so errors stay part of your score. <span class=\"kbd\">Tab</span> resets the test.</div>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"progress\"><div class=\"bar\" id=\"bar\"></div></div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"actions\"><button class=\"secondary\" id=\"reset\">Reset test</button><button class=\"primary\" id=\"finish\">Finish now</button></div>\n      <div class=\"result\" id=\"result\">\n        <h2>Session complete</h2>\n        <div class=\"resultgrid\">\n          <div class=\"resultcard\"><div class=\"small\">Final WPM</div><div class=\"big\" id=\"rWpm\">0</div></div>\n          <div class=\"resultcard\"><div class=\"small\">Accuracy</div><div class=\"big\" id=\"rAcc\">0%</div></div>\n          <div class=\"resultcard\"><div class=\"small\">Errors</div><div class=\"big\" id=\"rErr\">0</div></div>\n          <div class=\"resultcard\"><div class=\"small\">Characters</div><div class=\"big\" id=\"rChars\">0</div></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </section>\n \n    <div class=\"adslot\" aria-label=\"Advertisement\"><div class=\"adlabel\">Advertisement</div></div>\n \n    <footer class=\"footer\">Your recent best: <strong id=\"best\">0 WPM</strong> • stored only in this browser</footer>\n  </div>\n \n  <script>\n    const englishEasySeeds = [\n      \"Typing is a useful skill for school, work, and everyday computer tasks. Keep your hands relaxed and focus on the next word.\",\n      \"A steady rhythm helps you type with fewer mistakes. Read the words carefully and let your fingers move at a comfortable pace.\",\n      \"Practice for a few minutes every day. Small sessions can build confidence and make the keyboard feel more familiar.\",\n      \"Good posture makes long typing sessions easier. Sit comfortably, keep your shoulders relaxed, and look at the text instead of the keys.\",\n      \"Accuracy comes before speed. When your typing becomes clean and regular, your speed can grow without extra effort.\",\n      \"Use both hands and keep your fingers close to the home row. This simple habit can make common words easier to type.\",\n      \"A calm mind helps the hands stay steady. Take each word in order and avoid rushing when a sentence feels difficult.\",\n      \"Typing improves through repetition. Each practice session gives your fingers another chance to learn the right movement.\",\n      \"Look slightly ahead while you type. Reading the next few words early can help you keep a smooth and natural pace.\",\n      \"The best practice is regular practice. A short session today is more useful than waiting for a perfect time next week.\",\n    ];\n \n    const englishMediumSeeds = [\n      \"Learning to type well is less about forcing your fingers to move quickly and more about building a dependable rhythm. When each hand knows where to travel, attention can stay on the sentence instead of the keyboard. A calm pace also makes mistakes easier to notice, correct, and prevent on the next line.\",\n      \"A focused practice session gives the brain a simple job: recognize the next word, choose the right keys, and keep the rhythm moving. Over time, this sequence becomes automatic. That is why short, regular sessions often create stronger habits than occasional bursts of effort followed by long breaks.\",\n      \"Good posture quietly affects typing performance. Feet can rest naturally, shoulders can stay loose, and wrists can remain neutral while the fingers move. The goal is not to create a rigid position, but to remove unnecessary tension so that the hands can work comfortably for longer periods without feeling rushed.\",\n      \"Reading a little ahead is one of the easiest ways to make typing smoother. Instead of waiting for each word to finish before thinking about the next one, let your eyes preview the upcoming phrase. This creates a small buffer between reading and typing, which helps the rhythm remain steady when sentences become longer.\",\n      \"Accuracy deserves attention even when the goal is higher speed. A fast test filled with corrections can feel impressive for a moment, but clean keystrokes create a more useful foundation. When errors decrease, speed often follows naturally because fewer pauses are needed to repair the text.\",\n      \"Typing practice can also improve digital confidence. Writing an email, entering a form, preparing notes, or editing a document becomes less tiring when the keyboard feels familiar. The benefit is not only measured in words per minute; it appears in the ease with which ideas move from the mind to the screen.\",\n      \"Different punctuation marks create different movements across the keyboard. Commas, periods, quotation marks, brackets, and symbols may interrupt an easy rhythm until they become familiar. Including varied punctuation in practice makes real writing feel more predictable because the hands have already experienced those small changes in direction.\",\n      \"Long sentences are useful because they test more than speed. They require the typist to maintain attention, preserve spacing, remember punctuation, and keep a stable rhythm across several connected ideas. When a sentence feels difficult, slowing down slightly can reveal which movement or key combination is causing the hesitation.\",\n      \"A five-minute test is long enough to reveal habits that are invisible in a very short sprint. The first minute may feel energetic, the middle may settle into a routine, and the final minute can expose fatigue or loss of concentration. Reviewing the full session helps identify where consistency improves and where it starts to fall.\",\n      \"Technology changes quickly, but the keyboard remains an everyday tool for students, designers, developers, analysts, writers, and business teams. Better typing does not replace good thinking. It simply reduces the mechanical effort required to express that thinking, leaving more attention available for planning, checking, and communicating clearly.\",\n      \"A reliable practice routine does not need complicated equipment. A comfortable keyboard, a readable screen, and a few uninterrupted minutes are enough to begin. What matters most is repetition with intention. Each session should have one simple focus, such as cleaner spacing, fewer errors, smoother punctuation, or a steadier pace.\",\n      \"When a mistake happens, avoid turning it into a chain of mistakes. Notice it, correct it when the exercise requires correction, and continue with the next word. Staying emotionally neutral is useful because frustration adds another layer of distraction. The best response to an error is usually a calm return to the rhythm.\",\n      \"Typing rhythm is created by the spaces between actions as much as by the keystrokes themselves. If every word is attacked separately, the movement can feel jerky. Connecting small groups of words into phrases makes the hands flow more naturally. With practice, punctuation and capitalization can become part of that same continuous pattern.\",\n      \"Students often discover that typing speed matters during assignments because formatting, research, and revision all compete for limited time. Faster typing can shorten the mechanical part of the task, but accuracy remains important because a single incorrect word can change meaning. A balanced approach is therefore more useful than chasing a single number.\",\n      \"In office work, small improvements can add up across hundreds of messages and documents. A few extra words each minute may not sound dramatic, yet repeated every day they can save noticeable amounts of time. More importantly, comfortable typing reduces the feeling that routine digital tasks are constantly interrupting the thinking behind them.\",\n      \"Developers benefit from familiarity with numbers, punctuation, and repeated symbols because source code contains more than ordinary words. Brackets, slashes, colons, underscores, and operators appear frequently, and hesitation with these keys can break concentration. Practicing mixed text helps create smoother transitions between natural language and technical syntax.\",\n      \"The same principle applies to data entry. Tables, addresses, dates, names, and reference codes demand careful attention because accuracy is often more important than raw speed. A good practice paragraph can include varied word lengths and symbols so that the typist learns to stay precise even when the pattern changes unexpectedly.\",\n      \"Reading and typing are closely connected during a test. Strong readers often gain an advantage because they can recognize common word patterns before finishing every letter. This does not mean guessing. It means processing familiar combinations efficiently. Building a broad vocabulary can therefore make typing feel smoother even though vocabulary and keyboard skill are different abilities.\",\n      \"A clean desk can remove surprisingly small sources of distraction. Notifications, crowded windows, uncomfortable lighting, and constant background interruptions all compete for attention. A dedicated practice block creates a simple environment in which the typist can observe performance honestly and notice whether speed, accuracy, or consistency changes over time.\",\n      \"Progress is easier to understand when it is recorded. Tracking WPM, accuracy, errors, and consistency after each practice session turns a vague feeling into useful information. One unusual result does not say much by itself, so several sessions should be compared before deciding whether a habit is improving. Trends matter more than isolated peaks.\",\n      \"The keyboard should feel like a map rather than a puzzle. Home-row positioning gives the hands a reference point, while familiar finger patterns reduce the need to look down. Once the hands can return to that reference point naturally, reaching for distant keys becomes less disruptive. This is one reason structured drills can be valuable for beginners.\",\n      \"A useful exercise sometimes feels almost too easy. That is not necessarily a problem. Repeating comfortable patterns gives the brain a chance to automate them. Later, when more difficult words arrive, those familiar movements require less conscious attention. Skill grows from the combination of easy repetition and gradually increasing challenge.\",\n      \"Another useful method is to practice words that frequently cause hesitation. If the same combinations repeatedly slow you down, give them extra attention rather than simply repeating an entire test. Focused practice can isolate the problem and turn an awkward sequence into a familiar one. Then return to full paragraphs to measure whether the change holds.\",\n      \"Typing tests can become more interesting when the text covers different subjects. Travel, science, business, history, design, education, and everyday life all produce different vocabulary and sentence patterns. Variety prevents the fingers from memorizing one narrow set of phrases and encourages flexible skill that transfers to real writing.\",\n      \"Consistency is easier to maintain when the pace is sustainable. Starting at maximum speed may create a strong first minute but leave the final minutes filled with hesitation. A controlled beginning gives the hands time to settle. Once the rhythm feels stable, a small increase can be made without sacrificing accuracy. This approach turns the test into a steady climb rather than a short sprint.\",\n      \"Clear text layout also matters. Comfortable line spacing and a readable typeface make it easier for the eyes to track the current position. When the practice area separates paragraphs cleanly, the next block is easier to scan and the typist can understand how much text remains. Good interface design should support the task rather than compete with it.\",\n      \"An effective typing website should make the result understandable at a glance. WPM tells one story, accuracy tells another, and errors reveal where attention may have slipped. A final result that combines these measures gives a more complete picture than speed alone. Over time, the numbers can help set realistic goals for the next session.\",\n      \"Daily practice can be short and still be useful. Ten focused minutes may be enough to reinforce a technique, especially when the session has a clear purpose. A learner who practices consistently can gradually raise the level of difficulty without feeling overwhelmed. Small improvements repeated across many days can create a noticeable difference in confidence.\",\n      \"Typing also teaches a lesson about repetition. At first, a movement feels deliberate because the brain is choosing each step. After enough correct repetitions, the same movement becomes automatic and requires less conscious control. This shift is one reason practice should emphasize correct technique rather than simply producing as many keystrokes as possible.\",\n      \"When a paragraph contains an unfamiliar word, do not let the word dominate the entire session. Break it into familiar pieces, keep the hands moving, and continue. Over time, unusual spellings become easier to recognize. The objective is not to remove every difficult word, but to make the response to difficulty more controlled and less disruptive.\",\n      \"Working with longer passages can strengthen endurance. Short bursts can hide small problems because there is not enough time for fatigue to appear. A longer passage reveals whether the hands remain relaxed, whether accuracy stays stable, and whether reading ahead continues to work. That information can guide the next round of practice.\",\n      \"Real writing rarely consists of one perfect sentence repeated again and again. It contains names, numbers, punctuation, short phrases, long explanations, and occasional corrections. Practice that includes this variety is closer to everyday keyboard work. The more varied the exercise, the less likely the typist is to depend on memorized patterns.\",\n      \"A good benchmark is not simply the fastest score you have ever seen. It is the level you can reproduce with reasonable accuracy. Repeatable performance is more useful for planning because it represents a skill that can be relied upon. Once consistency improves, faster results become easier to pursue without making the keyboard feel chaotic.\",\n      \"For many learners, the biggest change comes from stopping the habit of looking down after every few words. Keeping the eyes on the text allows the fingers to use their learned positions without constant visual confirmation. The transition may feel uncomfortable at first, but repeated practice can gradually make the keyboard feel more predictable.\",\n      \"The beginning of a session should be treated as a warm-up rather than a race. The first few lines can help the hands settle into position and the eyes adjust to the pace of the text. Once the rhythm is established, speed becomes easier to control. This simple routine can also reduce the temptation to rush the opening seconds.\",\n      \"Typing accuracy is measured against the text, but concentration is measured by how consistently the hands follow the eyes. When attention breaks, errors often appear in clusters. A brief reset of posture, breathing, and focus can interrupt that pattern. There is no need for drama; a quiet return to the next word is enough.\",\n      \"Long-form practice is especially useful for people who write reports, documentation, articles, notes, or messages every day. These tasks demand sustained attention rather than a short burst of maximum speed. Training with several paragraphs helps the typist become comfortable with the feeling of continuous input and reduces the effort required to stay engaged.\",\n      \"A typing test can also be treated as a measurement tool. Run the same level on several days, keep the conditions roughly similar, and compare the results. If WPM rises while accuracy remains stable, the improvement is meaningful. If speed rises while accuracy falls sharply, the session may be showing a trade-off worth addressing before pushing further.\",\n      \"There is no universal ideal typing speed because different tasks have different demands. Someone entering codes may value precision, while a writer may care more about sustained rhythm. The useful target is therefore connected to the work itself. Practice should support the kinds of sentences, symbols, and input patterns that the person actually uses.\",\n      \"A well-designed practice passage can subtly teach patience. Each sentence provides another chance to correct technique, each paragraph offers a fresh rhythm, and the full session rewards consistency. The experience becomes less about proving a number and more about building a skill that feels dependable when the keyboard is part of everyday work.\",\n      \"Over time, familiar words begin to feel like single shapes rather than separate letters. The fingers still press individual keys, but the brain recognizes the pattern quickly. This is one of the clearest signs that practice is working. The same idea appears in music, sports, and other skills where repeated sequences become coordinated and efficient.\",\n      \"If the goal is to increase speed, make changes gradually. Raise the pace a little, then check whether accuracy remains within a comfortable range. If errors increase dramatically, reduce the pace and reinforce the pattern before trying again. Sustainable speed grows from controlled repetition, not from forcing the fingers beyond what the technique can support.\",\n      \"Practice text should feel relevant enough to hold attention. Sentences about useful ideas, familiar situations, or interesting subjects are easier to stay with than endless random syllables. Attention matters because typing is not purely mechanical. The eyes and brain are continuously processing meaning while the hands convert that meaning into movement.\",\n      \"When the paragraph on screen is complete and clearly separated, it becomes easier to navigate a long session. Each block acts as a visual landmark. Finishing one block creates a natural checkpoint before the next begins. This small bit of structure can make a large amount of practice text feel organized rather than overwhelming.\",\n      \"The final minute of a long test can reveal whether the practice method is working. If the pace stays stable and accuracy remains close to the beginning, endurance is improving. If performance drops sharply, the session can still be useful because it identifies an area for future work. Every result provides information that can shape the next practice round.\",\n      \"Typing is a practical skill with a simple feedback loop: read, press, observe, adjust, and repeat. The faster that loop becomes while staying accurate, the more fluent keyboard input feels. A clean practice environment makes that loop easier to observe, and a long enough passage gives the hands plenty of opportunities to reinforce the correct movement patterns.\",\n    ];\n \n    const englishHardSeeds = [\n      \"Efficient keyboarding requires deliberate repetition, accurate finger placement, and the discipline to maintain rhythm when punctuation becomes irregular.\",\n      \"Complex sentences challenge attention because commas, semicolons, quotation marks, parentheses, and dashes can interrupt an otherwise familiar sequence.\",\n      \"Professional writing often mixes short statements with longer clauses, technical vocabulary, numerical references, and abbreviations that demand precise keystrokes.\",\n      \"When a passage includes 2026, 3.14159, 98.6%, or a value such as $1,299.00, the typist must preserve every symbol while maintaining a stable cadence.\",\n      \"Advanced practice should expose weak transitions between letters, awkward reaches, capitalized words, apostrophes, and uncommon combinations that slow the hands.\",\n      \"A reliable typist does not chase speed blindly; instead, the typist monitors accuracy, anticipates the next phrase, and keeps unnecessary corrections from breaking the flow.\",\n      \"Technical documentation may contain file names like index.html, paths such as /assets/fonts/, code fragments, and identifiers including TypeMaster_v3, all within the same paragraph.\",\n      \"Fast input becomes genuinely useful when it survives difficult material: nested ideas, exact figures, mixed capitalization, symbols, and sentences with changing punctuation.\",\n      \"During an extended test, fatigue can expose small habits such as excessive thumb movement, tense wrists, delayed visual scanning, or repeated hesitation before punctuation.\",\n      \"The strongest improvement usually comes from measured practice: repeat difficult patterns, compare results, study error frequency, and then increase pace only when control remains consistent.\",\n    ];\n \n    function makeCorpus(seedList, minChars=34000, useVariants=true){\n      const shuffled=[...seedList].sort(()=>Math.random()-0.5);\n      const paragraphs=[];\n      let total=0, i=0;\n      const variants=[\n        \" During the next round, keep the same calm rhythm and watch for places where the fingers tend to hesitate.\",\n        \" As the exercise continues, read slightly ahead and allow the hands to complete each word without rushing.\",\n        \" This repetition is useful because deliberate movements gradually become dependable habits that need less attention.\",\n        \" The aim is not a perfect single attempt, but stronger control across the full practice session.\",\n        \" A longer passage also gives the eyes and hands more chances to settle into a consistent working pattern.\"\n      ];\n      while(total < minChars){\n        let para=shuffled[i % shuffled.length];\n        if(useVariants && i >= shuffled.length){\n          para += variants[i % variants.length];\n        }\n        paragraphs.push(para);\n        total += para.length + 2;\n        i++;\n      }\n      return paragraphs.sort(()=>Math.random()-0.5);\n    }\n \n    function makeHindiCorpus(seedList, minChars=34000){\n      return makeCorpus(seedList, minChars, false);\n    }\n \n    const texts = {\n      en: {\n        easy: [\n          'Practice makes typing faster and more comfortable every day. Keep your hands relaxed and focus on accuracy first.',\n          'A clear screen and steady rhythm can make typing feel simple. Read ahead, stay calm, and keep moving forward.'\n        ],\n        medium: [\n          'Good typing is a balance between speed, rhythm, and precision. Look at the next few words while your fingers finish the current one.',\n          'Consistent practice creates stronger muscle memory. Instead of chasing speed, build a smooth rhythm that you can repeat for five minutes.'\n        ],\n        hard: [\n          'Efficient typing depends on deliberate repetition, correct finger placement, and the discipline to recover from mistakes without breaking your rhythm.',\n          'When difficult punctuation, numbers, and longer sentences appear, maintain a steady pace and prioritize clean keystrokes over frantic bursts of speed.'\n        ]\n      },\n      hi: {\n        easy: [\n          'अच्छी टाइपिंग के लिए नियमित अभ्यास जरूरी है। पहले सही टाइप करने पर ध्यान दें और धीरे धीरे अपनी गति बढ़ाएं।',\n          'शांत रहें, शब्दों को आगे से पढ़ें और हाथों को आराम की स्थिति में रखें। नियमित अभ्यास से टाइपिंग आसान होती जाती है।'\n        ],\n        medium: [\n          'तेज और सही टाइपिंग केवल गति पर निर्भर नहीं करती। एक समान लय बनाए रखें और हर शब्द को ध्यान से टाइप करें।',\n          'पांच मिनट का लगातार अभ्यास मांसपेशियों की याददाश्त मजबूत करता है। गलतियों के बाद रुकने के बजाय लय को फिर से पकड़ें।'\n        ],\n        hard: [\n          'कठिन वाक्यों, विराम चिह्नों और लंबे शब्दों के दौरान गति से अधिक सटीकता को प्राथमिकता देना बेहतर अभ्यास माना जाता है।',\n          'जब आपकी उंगलियां सही कुंजी तक सहजता से पहुंचने लगें, तब धीरे धीरे गति बढ़ाएं और पूरे परीक्षण में एक स्थिर ताल बनाए रखें।'\n        ]\n      }\n    };\n    const $ = id => document.getElementById(id);\n    const els = { language:$('language'), duration:$('duration'), level:$('level'), newText:$('newText'), mode:$('modeLabel'), quote:$('quote'), input:$('input'), wpm:$('wpm'), accuracy:$('accuracy'), errors:$('errors'), time:$('time'), timer:$('timer'), reset:$('reset'), finish:$('finish'), result:$('result'), rWpm:$('rWpm'), rAcc:$('rAcc'), rErr:$('rErr'), rChars:$('rChars'), bar:$('bar'), best:$('best'), corpusInfo:$('corpusInfo') };\n    let paras=[], charEls=[], prevLen=0, target='', started=false, finished=false, startTime=0, timerId=null, duration=300, lastSnapshot={wpm:0,accuracy:100,errors:0,chars:0};\n \n    function pickText(){\n      const lang=els.language.value, level=els.level.value;\n      if(lang==='en'){\n        const bank = level==='easy' ? englishEasySeeds : level==='hard' ? englishHardSeeds : englishMediumSeeds;\n        paras=makeCorpus(bank, 34000);\n      } else {\n        const arr=texts[lang][level];\n        paras=makeHindiCorpus(arr, 12000);\n      }\n      target=paras.map((p,i)=>i<paras.length-1?p+' ':p).join(''); buildQuote(); updateMode();\n    }\n    function updateMode(){ const langText=els.language.options[els.language.selectedIndex].text; const levelText=els.level.options[els.level.selectedIndex].text; els.mode.textContent = `${langText} • ${levelText}`; els.corpusInfo.textContent = els.language.value==='en' ? '34K+ characters • randomized paragraphs' : '12K+ characters • randomized paragraphs'; }\n    function buildQuote(){\nlet html='';\nparas.forEach((p,pi)=>{\nconst text=pi<paras.length-1?p+' ':p;\nlet inner='';\nfor(let j=0;j<text.length;j++){\nconst ch=text[j];\nconst safe=ch.replace(/[&<>\"']/g,m=>({'&':'&amp;','<':'&lt;','>':'&gt;','\"':'&quot;',\"'\":'&#39;'}[m]));\ninner+=`<span>${safe}</span>`;\n}\nhtml+=`<div class=\"para\">${inner}</div>`;\n});\nels.quote.innerHTML=html; els.quote.scrollTop=0;\ncharEls=Array.from(els.quote.querySelectorAll('span')); prevLen=0;\nif(charEls[0]) charEls[0].className='current';\n}\nfunction updateQuote(typed){\nconst n=typed.length;\nif(charEls[prevLen]) charEls[prevLen].className='';\nfor(let i=Math.min(prevLen,n);i<n && i<charEls.length;i++) charEls[i].className = typed[i]===target[i] ? 'correct' : 'wrong';\nfor(let i=n;i<prevLen && i<charEls.length;i++) charEls[i].className='';\nconst cur=charEls[n];\nif(cur){\ncur.className='current';\nconst r=cur.getBoundingClientRect(), q=els.quote.getBoundingClientRect();\nif(r.bottom>q.bottom-40||r.top<q.top) els.quote.scrollTop += r.top-q.top-60;\n}\nprevLen=n;\n}\nfunction fmt(sec){sec=Math.max(0,Math.ceil(sec)); return `${Math.floor(sec/60)}:${String(sec%60).padStart(2,'0')}`}\n    function calculate(typed, elapsed){\n      let correct=0, errors=0;\n      for(let i=0;i<typed.length;i++){\n        if(typed[i]===target[i]) correct++; else errors++;\n      }\n      const minutes=Math.max(elapsed,3)/60;\n      const wpm=Math.round((correct/5)/minutes);\n      const accuracy=typed.length ? Math.round((correct/typed.length)*100) : 100;\n      return {wpm,accuracy,errors,chars:typed.length};\n    }\n    function updateStats(){\n      const typed=els.input.value;\n      const elapsed=started ? (Math.min(performance.now()-startTime, duration*1000)/1000) : 0;\n      lastSnapshot=calculate(typed, elapsed || 0.25);\n      els.wpm.textContent=lastSnapshot.wpm;\n      els.accuracy.textContent=`${lastSnapshot.accuracy}%`;\n      els.errors.textContent=lastSnapshot.errors;\n      const remain=duration-elapsed;\n      els.time.textContent=fmt(remain);\n      els.timer.textContent=fmt(remain);\n      els.timer.classList.toggle('urgent', remain<=30 && remain>0);\n      els.bar.style.width=`${Math.min(100,(typed.length/Math.max(1,target.length))*100)}%`;\n      if(typed.length>=target.length && !finished) finishTest();\n    }\n    function start(){\n      if(started||finished) return;\n      started=true; startTime=performance.now();\n      timerId=setInterval(()=>{\n        updateStats();\n        if(performance.now()-startTime>=duration*1000) finishTest();\n      },100);\n    }\n    function finishTest(){\n      if(finished) return;\n      finished=true; clearInterval(timerId); timerId=null;\n      const elapsed=Math.min((performance.now()-startTime)/1000,duration);\n      const typed=els.input.value;\n      const snap=calculate(typed, Math.max(elapsed,0.25)); lastSnapshot=snap;\n      els.input.blur(); els.input.disabled=true;\n      els.rWpm.textContent=snap.wpm; els.rAcc.textContent=`${snap.accuracy}%`; els.rErr.textContent=snap.errors; els.rChars.textContent=snap.chars;\n      els.result.classList.add('show'); els.timer.textContent='0:00'; els.time.textContent='0:00'; els.timer.classList.remove('urgent'); els.timer.classList.add('done');\n      const best=Math.max(Number(localStorage.getItem('typemasterBest')||0),snap.wpm); localStorage.setItem('typemasterBest',best); els.best.textContent=`${best} WPM`;\n    }\n    function resetTest(){\n      clearInterval(timerId); timerId=null; started=false; finished=false; startTime=0; duration=Number(els.duration.value);\n      els.input.disabled=false; els.input.value=''; els.wpm.textContent='0'; els.accuracy.textContent='100%'; els.errors.textContent='0'; els.time.textContent=fmt(duration); els.timer.textContent=fmt(duration); els.timer.className='timer'; els.bar.style.width='0%'; els.result.classList.remove('show');\n      pickText();\n    }\n    els.input.addEventListener('input',()=>{ if(!started) start(); updateQuote(els.input.value); updateStats(); });\n    els.input.addEventListener('keydown',e=>{\n      if(e.key==='Tab'){e.preventDefault(); resetTest(); els.input.focus(); return;}\n      const blockedKeys = ['Backspace','Delete','ArrowLeft','ArrowRight','ArrowUp','ArrowDown','Home','End'];\n      const combo = e.ctrlKey || e.metaKey;\n      if(blockedKeys.includes(e.key) || (combo && ['a','x','c','v','z','y'].includes(e.key.toLowerCase()))){\n        e.preventDefault();\n      }\n    });\n    els.input.addEventListener('paste',e=>e.preventDefault());\n    els.input.addEventListener('cut',e=>e.preventDefault());\n    els.input.addEventListener('drop',e=>e.preventDefault());\n    [els.language,els.duration,els.level].forEach(el=>el.addEventListener('change',resetTest));\n    els.newText.addEventListener('click',()=>{pickText(); els.input.focus()}); els.reset.addEventListener('click',()=>{resetTest(); els.input.focus()}); els.finish.addEventListener('click',finishTest);\n    els.best.textContent=`${Number(localStorage.getItem('typemasterBest')||0)} WPM`;\n    resetTest();\n  </script>\n</body>\n</html>\n \n\n"
      }
    }
  ]
